      "items": [
        {
          "key": "cashback_caps_effective_2026_04_01",
          "description": "From 1 April 2026, online cashback is capped at ₹2,000 per statement cycle, offline/POS cashback is capped at ₹2,000 per statement cycle, and aggregate cashback is capped at ₹4,000 per statement cycle.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/cashback-revised\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "cashback_posting_basis",
          "description": "Cashback accrues on the transaction posting/settlement date rather than the effective transaction date, using the cashback structure applicable when the transaction posts.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/faq/cashback-sbi-card-faq.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "cashback_forfeiture_and_closure",
          "description": "If the card is voluntarily closed, earned cashback may be redeemed within 30 days of closure; otherwise it lapses. On cancellation for another reason, earned cashback is forfeited. Cashback is also forfeited following more than 90 days of payment delinquency, settlement of outstanding dues, fraud determined by SBICPSL, or specified regulatory events.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/sbi-card-en/assets/docs/pdf/cashback-tnc-booklet.pdf\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "cashback_network_identification",
          "description": "Online transactions are identified using online indicators sent by card networks and the acquirer; transactions not categorized as online are treated as offline. Network MCC definitions may change.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/sbi-card-en/assets/docs/pdf/cashback-tnc-booklet.pdf\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "education_payment_fee_detail",
          "description": "From 1 November 2025, education payments through third-party apps such as CRED, Cheq and MobiKwik attract a 1% fee. Direct payments to colleges or schools through their websites or POS machines do not attract this fee. Education MCCs identified on a best-effort basis are 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249 and 8299.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "wallet_load_fee_detail",
          "description": "From 1 November 2025, a 1% fee applies to every wallet load transaction exceeding ₹1,000. Wallet transactions are identified under MCCs 6540 and 6541 on a best-effort basis.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "rent_payment_fee_detail",
          "description": "All transactions towards payment of rent through a merchant attract a ₹199 processing fee plus applicable taxes. MCC 6513 is used to identify rent transactions on a best-effort basis.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "utility_payment_fee_detail",
          "description": "If aggregate utility payments in a billing cycle exceed ₹50,000, a 1% fee applies to the total utility payments in that billing cycle. Utility payments are identified under MCC 4900 on a best-effort basis.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "cash_advance_limit_detail",
          "description": "Cash advance is part of the overall credit limit. The MITC states a maximum cash withdrawal of ₹15,000 per day on MCC 6011 (ATM withdrawals), subject to cash advance limit availability; cash advance is unavailable for MCC 6010 over-the-counter cash disbursement. The general schedule also specifies cash advance up to 80% of the credit limit.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "cash_payment_fee",
          "description": "Cash payment of SBI credit card dues at select SBI branches carries a ₹250 service fee plus applicable taxes.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "balance_transfer",
          "description": "Balance Transfer facility can transfer another bank's credit-card outstanding. The Cashback SBI Card terms state a minimum transfer amount of ₹5,000 and maximum of up to 75% of available credit limit, with processing fee as applicable. A 60-day balance transfer option is shown at 0% interest and a 180-day option at 1.7% per month, with applicable processing fee and restrictions.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/sbi-card-en/assets/docs/pdf/cashback-tnc-booklet.pdf\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "minimum_finance_charge",
          "description": "Minimum finance charge is ₹25 per applicable transaction/cash advance when revolving finance charges apply, exclusive of applicable taxes.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "payment_dishonor_fee",
          "description": "Payment dishonor fee is 2% of the payment amount subject to a minimum of ₹500.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "late_payment_additional_charge",
          "description": "An additional ₹100 late-payment charge is levied when Minimum Amount Due is missed by the due date for two consecutive cycles, continuing each payment cycle until MAD is cleared.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "cashback_customer_service",
          "description": "SBI Card helpline numbers published in the MITC are 39 02 02 02 with the local STD prefix and 1860 180 1290.",
          "source": "https://www.sbicard.com/en/most-important-terms-and-conditions.page\n"
        },
        {
          "key": "contactless_operation",
